    "heightBasis": "Retained exact-QID OSM way27044968/Q1630170 matches current main35184399133800. All6 raw whole vertices and current dome19/tower4+4 component vertices and full tags remain exact after rigid rotation with no rescale. Main20m and dome/towers30m heights are PMTiles controls for complete components, not offsets added on top of the main height. West twin-tower facade versus eastward nave/dome signs the retained axis. Main body: estimated low aisle walls12m/parapet13.2m, central nave and transept walls17.8m with low roof20m; full west screen20m/central pediment23.3m/finial24.3m. Towers: lower clock shaft20m, open bell tier20..25.2m, hood25.2..26.3m, curved stone spire26.3..29m/cross30m. Dome: estimated octagonal drum18..25m, low faceted metal canopy25..27.9m, lantern27.8..29.4m/cross30m. Drum center[6.614,-0.708]m/radius9.1m is derived from mapped circular control; octagonal shape/phase and roof partitions are picture estimates. Portals, clocks, window rhythm, stone pilasters/capitals and scrolls are approximate. No survey or engineering accuracy claimed.",
    "scope": "Individual St. Paul’s Cathedral, Mdina: warm Maltese limestone Baroque west front with paired clock/bell towers and curved stone spires, central triangular pediment/cross, paired pilasters, three recessed wooden portals and large upper arched window. Broad lower flat-roof aisles, eastward central nave/crossing, large octagonal windowed drum, low weathered metal dome with stone ribs/scrolls and small lantern/cross. Sparse side windows, cornices, stone diamonds/crest and short front steps. Five existing shared ashlar/limestone/granite/standing-seam-metal/wood graphs, linear tints, metric UVs, flat architectural normals and four browser levels. Exact carving/heraldry/clock numerals, full interiors/bells, hidden rear windows/roof joins and surveyed plaza/thresholds remain approximate or excluded."
